      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62671,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 125,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Ovarian hilus</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:42:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62672,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 125,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Androgenic and estrogenic manifestations are possible. An increased number of Leydig cells has been observed in association with endometrioid carcinomas of the uterus {30428390}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:42:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62673,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 125,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The lesion is most commonly seen in pregnant, perimenopausal, and postmenopausal women.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:42:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62674,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 125,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>See below.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:42:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62675,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 125,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Leydig cell hyperplasia can be a physiological event due to elevated serum hCG or LH. Derivation from hilus nerves has been postulated {28127725}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:42:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62676,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 125,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Leydig cell hyperplasia is not grossly visible.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:42:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62677,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 125,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Histopathology reveals nodules of Leydig cells within the ovarian hilus that may encircle nerve fibres and rete ovarii. The cells are typically polygonal, with central round nuclei showing prominent nucleoli and abundant eosinophilic cytoplasm, which may contain Reinke crystals {28127725}. There may be associated stromal hyperplasia or stromal hyperthecosis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:42:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62678,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 125,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:42:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
